00:53:07,250 --> 00:53:08,250
Hey, hey!

1311
00:53:09,750 --> 00:53:11,750
Cross your legs, Robert, you
can see the squirrel.

1312
00:53:15,760 --> 00:53:18,260
I wanna go home with
that armadillo.

1313
00:53:25,770 --> 00:53:27,270
Hey buddy, you want an apple?

1314
00:53:27,270 --> 00:53:28,770
(laughs) I kid.

1315
00:53:30,770 --> 00:53:32,770
Say, you got a match, Robert?

1316
00:53:32,770 --> 00:53:33,780
Yeah.

1317
00:53:33,770 --> 00:53:35,770
William Shatner and
Robert Vaughan.

1318
00:53:35,780 --> 00:53:38,280
Lookit, he does got-
He has matches.

1319
00:53:38,280 --> 00:53:39,780
Unbelievable.

1320
00:53:42,280 --> 00:53:43,790
I hope they don't see me.

1321
00:53:43,780 --> 00:53:46,780
I could get in big trouble, this
is a national park.

1322
00:53:47,790 --> 00:53:50,290
(blowing air)

1323
00:53:57,800 --> 00:53:59,800
I am powerless over pyromania

1324
00:53:59,800 --> 00:54:02,300
and my life has become
unmanageable.

1325
00:54:05,810 --> 00:54:10,310
I ate it with Fava beans and a
nice Chianti. (slurping)

1326
00:54:10,310 --> 00:54:11,810
Wait a minute, don't eat it,

1327
00:54:11,810 --> 00:54:14,820
Corman wants to use that for a
monster in his next movie.

1328
00:54:14,810 --> 00:54:16,310
Hey, you think that fire's
big enough, Bob?

1329
00:54:16,820 --> 00:54:17,320
Whoa.

1330
00:54:24,820 --> 00:54:26,820
(laughing)

1331
00:54:26,830 --> 00:54:30,330
He looks like H.R. Pufnstuf
after a fiery car wreck.

1332
00:54:30,330 --> 00:54:32,830
Something goofy this way comes.

1333
00:54:34,330 --> 00:54:35,330
It's me!

1334
00:54:35,840 --> 00:54:37,340
I'm Trumpy!

1335
00:54:37,340 --> 00:54:38,340
Oh yeah.

1336
00:54:43,340 --> 00:54:45,840
Oh that's okay, don't say hi.

1337
00:54:48,350 --> 00:54:51,850
I hate to eat and run, but
(laughs) goodbye.

1338
00:54:51,850 --> 00:54:53,860
Bob, Bob, Bob of the Jungle,

1339
00:54:53,850 --> 00:54:55,350
friend to you and me.

1340
00:54:57,860 --> 00:54:59,860
Watch out for that tree.

1341
00:54:59,860 --> 00:55:01,360
I guess so.

1342
00:55:04,360 --> 00:55:06,360
The blood is clean.

1343
00:55:06,370 --> 00:55:08,370
Hyman Roth?

1344
00:55:09,370 --> 00:55:10,870
What the heck is he
talking about?

1345
00:55:10,870 --> 00:55:12,370
No clue.

1346
00:55:12,370 --> 00:55:13,880
He asks after his son.

1347
00:55:15,880 --> 00:55:18,880
Oh, he just had a Sealy
Posturpedic morning.

1348
00:55:18,880 --> 00:55:19,380
Yeah!

1349
00:55:20,380 --> 00:55:21,380
The boy.

1350
00:55:21,380 --> 00:55:23,390
I'm mad about the boy.

1351
00:55:23,380 --> 00:55:24,880
Bring him.

1352
00:55:25,890 --> 00:55:27,390
He is not here.

1353
00:55:27,890 --> 00:55:29,390
Where then?

1354
00:55:29,390 --> 00:55:30,390
Beyond the river.

1355
00:55:30,390 --> 00:55:34,400
And through the woods, to
grandmother's house he went.

1356
00:55:34,390 --> 00:55:35,890
A time ago.

1357
00:55:35,900 --> 00:55:37,900
How long is he gone?

1358
00:55:37,900 --> 00:55:40,900
Uh, a fireball and
two stones ago.

1359
00:55:40,900 --> 00:55:43,410
Two risings of the sun.

1360
00:55:43,400 --> 00:55:44,900
A couple of days, then.

1361
00:55:44,900 --> 00:55:45,900
Who knows of this?

1362
00:55:45,910 --> 00:55:46,910
All the clan.

1363
00:55:46,910 --> 00:55:48,410
He took others with him.

1364
00:55:48,410 --> 00:55:50,910
They're all talking about it.

1365
00:55:52,910 --> 00:55:54,420
Aw, if it's not one
thing it's another

1366
00:55:54,410 --> 00:55:55,910
around this crazy tribe.

1367
00:55:55,920 --> 00:55:59,920
(grunts) Oh boy, chili
peppers burn my gut.

1368
00:55:59,920 --> 00:56:01,920
Gotta go see a man about a dog.

1369
00:56:11,360 --> 00:56:13,360
Your son has broken the law.

1370
00:56:13,370 --> 00:56:14,870
He is beyond the river.

1371
00:56:14,870 --> 00:56:16,870
And he's totally off script!

1372
00:56:17,370 --> 00:56:19,870
Your blood will bring the
death to visit us!

1373
00:56:19,870 --> 00:56:22,380
As it was told in times past.

1374
00:56:22,370 --> 00:56:23,370
In the People column.

1375
00:56:23,380 --> 00:56:24,380
Boy.

1376
00:56:24,380 --> 00:56:26,880
Boy, crazy boy!

1377
00:56:27,380 --> 00:56:28,380
Tell me.

1378
00:56:28,380 --> 00:56:30,890
Your son led us to go
beyond the river.

1379
00:56:30,880 --> 00:56:32,880
We saw terrible things.

1380
00:56:32,890 --> 00:56:34,890
Great beasts fighting.

1381
00:56:34,890 --> 00:56:35,890
F Troop reruns.

1382
00:56:35,890 --> 00:56:37,390
One of us was taken
by the earth.

1383
00:56:37,390 --> 00:56:38,390
Which one?

1384
00:56:38,390 --> 00:56:40,400
- Lumpy, Mr. Cleaver. - A
fair-haired boy.

1385
00:56:40,390 --> 00:56:41,390
And my son?

1386
00:56:41,390 --> 00:56:43,390
We left him there.

1387
00:56:44,400 --> 00:56:45,400
Left him?

1388
00:56:45,400 --> 00:56:47,400
He didn't follow us back.

1389
00:56:47,400 --> 00:56:48,400
He's dead.

1390
00:56:48,400 --> 00:56:51,410
But the evil will come
all the same.

1391
00:56:51,400 --> 00:56:54,400
He's brought it down upon us.

1392
00:56:54,410 --> 00:56:55,410
No!

1393
00:56:55,410 --> 00:56:58,410
I will find him, bring him back!

1394
00:56:58,410 --> 00:57:00,920
I will leave no stone unturned,

1395
00:57:00,910 --> 00:57:04,410
starting with this one, yeah.

1396
00:57:04,420 --> 00:57:07,920
Wait, this is no time to
make flapjacks!

1397
00:57:07,920 --> 00:57:10,430
Okay, I want you to go deep.

1398
00:57:12,420 --> 00:57:13,420
Hm?

1399
00:57:13,430 --> 00:57:15,430
Run around in a circle.

1400
00:57:15,430 --> 00:57:16,930
At the sun's third rising.

1401
00:57:16,930 --> 00:57:19,430
We'll call it Wednesday,
about noon.

1402
00:57:19,430 --> 00:57:20,440
Nice.

1403
00:57:24,440 --> 00:57:26,440
Elias, Mr. Waverly!

1404
00:57:26,440 --> 00:57:27,440
Thrush.

1405
00:57:30,440 --> 00:57:32,940
Hey, he invented the hangover.

1406
00:57:34,450 --> 00:57:37,450
(vomiting noises)

1407
00:57:40,950 --> 00:57:44,950
I think that I will never see a
poem as lovely as, ow!

1408
00:57:44,960 --> 00:57:49,960
(laughing dumbly)

1409
00:57:52,970 --> 00:57:54,970
Branch is funny.

1410
00:58:01,470 --> 00:58:04,970
I'm just a morning person,
what can I say?

1411
00:58:07,480 --> 00:58:10,490
Oh, he's inventing the violin.

1412
00:58:11,980 --> 00:58:13,480
Or the loom.

1413
00:58:17,560 --> 00:58:20,560
Gotta figure a way to pluck
these eyebrows.

1414
00:58:25,560 --> 00:58:26,560
Oh, come on.

1415
00:58:27,570 --> 00:58:30,070
Oh, wait, no, come on, let me
get this straight.

1416
00:58:30,070 --> 00:58:33,580
He got hit on the tree, and he
got smart, right?

1417
00:58:33,570 --> 00:58:34,570
Yep.

1418
00:58:35,070 --> 00:58:36,070
Uh huh.

1419
00:58:37,580 --> 00:58:38,450
Hm.

1420
00:58:39,810 --> 00:58:44,320
And it's a good thing for me, I
have my trusty dental floss!

1421
00:58:44,320 --> 00:58:47,320
Why I'm not sure, but I think
I've found the beginnings

1422
00:58:47,320 --> 00:58:49,320
of an Olympic event!

1423
00:58:55,330 --> 00:58:58,330
(humming)

1424
00:58:58,830 --> 00:59:00,340
Oh, petting zoo.

1425
00:59:00,330 --> 00:59:01,830
That seems nice.

1426
00:59:01,830 --> 00:59:03,330
Yeah, sweet.

1427
00:59:03,840 --> 00:59:05,340
You will die, doe.

1428
00:59:05,840 --> 00:59:07,840
Ross all over again.

1429
00:59:08,840 --> 00:59:11,350
So anyways, as I was saying,
there are three...

1430
00:59:11,340 --> 00:59:15,340
(dramatic music)

1431
00:59:16,850 --> 00:59:18,850
Honey, that was swell.

1432
00:59:18,850 --> 00:59:20,360
Well, see you later, dear.

1433
00:59:20,350 --> 00:59:23,350
I'm gonna go play Mahjong with
Betty and Frieda.

1434
00:59:25,360 --> 00:59:27,860
Don't you guys ever sleep?

1435
00:59:31,360 --> 00:59:34,360
Hey, he invented the mink stole!

1436
00:59:34,370 --> 00:59:35,370
That's a stiff deer.

1437
00:59:35,370 --> 00:59:36,870
Deerskin jacket.

1438
00:59:37,370 --> 00:59:41,380
Uh oh, Rob, your dad
found your stash!

1439
00:59:41,370 --> 00:59:42,870
Look at all of it!

1440
00:59:48,880 --> 00:59:52,390
Uh oh, they're on a collision
course for wackiness,

1441
00:59:52,380 --> 00:59:56,380
when Junior meets dad it's all
mixed up! (laughs goofily)

1442
00:59:59,390 --> 01:00:00,900
Marmaduke, no!

1443
01:00:00,890 --> 01:00:02,390
Wait, how can there
be Great Danes

1444
01:00:02,390 --> 01:00:04,890
when there isn't even
a Denmark yet?

1445
01:00:17,410 --> 01:00:20,420
That's a nice Chicago Cutlery
knife he's sporting there.

1446
01:00:22,410 --> 01:00:25,410
Bingo, Benji, Tramp, and Toto.

1447
01:00:26,420 --> 01:00:27,920
Toto too?

1448
01:00:27,920 --> 01:00:28,920
Uh huh.

1449
01:00:33,430 --> 01:00:35,430
Did he steal that from
an elk's lodge?

1450
01:00:37,430 --> 01:00:40,440
Oh here, take the deer, I gotta
see a man about a...

1451
01:00:40,430 --> 01:00:42,930
(barking)

1452
01:00:42,940 --> 01:00:45,440
Wait a minute, this is fake,
the deer's fake!

1453
01:00:45,440 --> 01:00:47,440
Get that guy, after him!

1454
01:00:54,950 --> 01:00:55,950
Ah, man bites dog.

1455
01:00:55,950 --> 01:00:57,950
I read about this in the paper.

1456
01:00:59,950 --> 01:01:00,960
Ooh!

1457
01:01:00,950 --> 01:01:02,950
All dogs go to heaven.

1458
01:01:02,960 --> 01:01:04,460
Bowser, no!

1459
01:01:05,460 --> 01:01:07,460
Come here, you, your
mother is furious.

1460
01:01:07,460 --> 01:01:08,460
But I was evolving, Dad!

1461
01:01:08,460 --> 01:01:09,960
Shut up, shut up,
we're going home.

1462
01:01:09,960 --> 01:01:11,470
Wait until your ancestors get.

1463
01:01:11,460 --> 01:01:12,460
We live by the word.

1464
01:01:12,460 --> 01:01:13,460
Grease is the word.

1465
01:01:13,470 --> 01:01:14,470
We die without it.

1466
01:01:14,470 --> 01:01:16,470
Oh, he's a
Precambrian evangelist.

1467
01:01:16,470 --> 01:01:17,470
Mhm.

1468
01:01:17,470 --> 01:01:18,970
It is told that the
breaker of the law

1469
01:01:19,470 --> 01:01:20,980
must be put to death.

1470
01:01:20,970 --> 01:01:22,470
Doodly doodly doo!

1471
01:01:22,470 --> 01:01:23,470
Wow, a swish pan!

1472
01:01:23,480 --> 01:01:24,980
They can use that later in
Man From Uncle!

1473
01:01:26,480 --> 01:01:29,480
Evil gods will come
down to kill!

1474
01:01:29,480 --> 01:01:31,490
As in times past.

1475
01:01:31,480 --> 01:01:33,480
Notice how I punched up the
word kill there?

1476
01:01:33,490 --> 01:01:34,990
That was my idea.

1477
01:01:34,990 --> 01:01:36,490
The keeper of the law
knows this is truth.

1478
01:01:36,490 --> 01:01:38,490
(snoring)

1479
01:01:38,490 --> 01:01:39,990
Wake up.

1480
01:01:39,990 --> 01:01:42,000
The son of the symbol
maker must die.

1481
01:01:42,490 --> 01:01:45,490
Hey, couldn't he just do some
community service instead?

1482
01:01:45,500 --> 01:01:46,500
(people shouting)

1483
01:01:46,500 --> 01:01:48,000
Hey!

1484
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:49,500
Hey I don't know, it's new, I
just thought of it.

1485
01:01:49,500 --> 01:01:51,010
Hey?

1486
01:01:51,000 --> 01:01:53,000
Each of us have wandered
after the truth.

1487
01:01:53,010 --> 01:01:55,510
The word tells us that
the law is truth.

1488
01:01:55,510 --> 01:01:56,510
Mhm.

1489
01:01:56,510 --> 01:01:58,510
- This one has broken the law. -
The word or the law?

1490
01:01:58,510 --> 01:02:00,520
But still the gods have not come

1491
01:02:00,510 --> 01:02:03,010
as it's told they will come.

1492
01:02:03,020 --> 01:02:05,520
Door number one! Take
the curtain!

1493
01:02:05,520 --> 01:02:07,020
Evil's near us.

1494
01:02:07,020 --> 01:02:09,520
The clan will be no more.

1495
01:02:09,520 --> 01:02:13,530
I say only to wait
until it does come.

1496
01:02:13,530 --> 01:02:16,030
And I say it must be kept
from the people

1497
01:02:16,030 --> 01:02:17,530
by another death!

1498
01:02:17,530 --> 01:02:18,030
Ooh.

1499
01:02:18,530 --> 01:02:20,540
The word of the law is truth.

1500
01:02:20,530 --> 01:02:25,530
Let the guilty one be as
dead until manhood.

1501
01:02:25,540 --> 01:02:28,040
Gee, it's kind of like
Inherit the Wind.

1502
01:02:28,040 --> 01:02:29,540
Only backwards.

1503
01:02:29,540 --> 01:02:30,550
No, no!

1504
01:02:31,040 --> 01:02:34,040
♪ No no, no no no no,
no no no no

1505
01:02:34,050 --> 01:02:35,550
(laughs)

1506
01:02:35,550 --> 01:02:39,050
It shall be as the
symbol maker says!

1507
01:02:39,050 --> 01:02:40,560
Hey, don't I get an appeal?

1508
01:02:43,560 --> 01:02:46,060
(chuckles) An amateur
photographer caught this footage

1509
01:02:46,060 --> 01:02:47,560
of early policeman.

1510
01:02:49,560 --> 01:02:51,070
(muffled cries)

1511
01:02:51,060 --> 01:02:53,560
Stop it, Dad, uncle Bob is
picking on me again!

1512
01:02:53,570 --> 01:02:55,570
(muffled groans)

1513
01:02:56,570 --> 01:02:58,070
Oh, this must be

1514
01:02:58,070 --> 01:03:01,080
where professional
wrestling got its start.

1515
01:03:06,080 --> 01:03:09,580
Ah right, like you had good luck
with that thing before.

1516
01:03:17,090 --> 01:03:20,600
Why couldn't I just get
cast in Daddy-O?

1517
01:03:20,590 --> 01:03:25,590
(humming over dramatic music)

1518
01:03:32,100 --> 01:03:32,600
Enough!

1519
01:03:33,610 --> 01:03:37,110
(fun futuristic music)

1520
01:03:40,880 --> 01:03:41,880
Hm?

1521
01:03:43,380 --> 01:03:46,890
Oh, sorry everybody, I'm sorry.

1522
01:03:47,390 --> 01:03:48,890
What?

1523
01:03:49,890 --> 01:03:51,890
What did I do? He started it!

1524
01:03:52,890 --> 01:03:54,400
All right folks, show's over,

1525
01:03:54,390 --> 01:03:57,390
nothing to see here,
everybody go home.

1526
01:03:57,400 --> 01:03:58,400
We should have left early.

1527
01:03:58,400 --> 01:04:00,400
Now there's gonna be
a traffic jam.

1528
01:04:05,900 --> 01:04:08,400
Oh, suddenly I'm the jerk.

1529
01:04:11,910 --> 01:04:13,410
Poor sap.

1530
01:04:15,410 --> 01:04:16,910
(sweet music)

1531
01:04:16,920 --> 01:04:17,420
Oh, hey.

1532
01:04:17,420 --> 01:04:18,920
Esther Williams.

1533
01:04:19,920 --> 01:04:22,920
Now wait a minute,
she's got buttons?

1534
01:04:22,920 --> 01:04:25,430
No word for day, but
she's got buttons.

1535
01:04:25,420 --> 01:04:26,420
Terrific.

1536
01:04:27,930 --> 01:04:28,930
Say.

1537
01:04:29,430 --> 01:04:31,430
Hey, he's playing a Fudgicle!

1538
01:04:31,430 --> 01:04:32,430
Fudgsicle.

1539
01:04:32,430 --> 01:04:34,440
I always called it Fudgicle.

1540
01:04:34,930 --> 01:04:36,430
Sounds like the theme song

1541
01:04:36,440 --> 01:04:38,440
from Please Don't Eat
the Daisies.

1542
01:04:42,440 --> 01:04:44,950
He's gonna eat it later,
it's made of wax.

1543
01:04:44,940 --> 01:04:46,440
You dropped your soap! (laughs)

1544
01:04:46,450 --> 01:04:47,950
Just kidding.

1545
01:04:50,450 --> 01:04:51,450
Say.

1546
01:04:53,950 --> 01:04:56,450
I know you're not to give voice
to me or I to you.

1547
01:04:56,460 --> 01:04:58,460
But I can stand here and
watch you, right?

1548
01:04:58,460 --> 01:05:00,960
Listen to this voice, then.

1549
01:05:01,460 --> 01:05:04,470
(blows flute)

1550
01:05:04,460 --> 01:05:07,960
Oh, I Talked To the Wind
by King Crimson!

1551
01:05:11,970 --> 01:05:15,480
Actually, I call this one
Opus One, Number One.

1552
01:05:23,480 --> 01:05:25,990
Um, like, do you know any Tull?

1553
01:05:28,990 --> 01:05:31,490
That voice I've heard at night.

1554
01:05:31,490 --> 01:05:32,990
In the life of dreams.

1555
01:05:32,990 --> 01:05:35,000
His skirt's shorter than hers.

1556
01:05:35,490 --> 01:05:37,490
I came to find it
beyond the river.

1557
01:05:37,500 --> 01:05:40,000
It is not a bad place that gives
the voice of dreams.

1558
01:05:40,000 --> 01:05:42,500
What are you, Carl Jung
all of a sudden?

1559
01:05:42,500 --> 01:05:45,010
There are strange things.

1560
01:05:45,000 --> 01:05:49,000
So I wonder how many strange
things there are,

1561
01:05:49,010 --> 01:05:51,510
beyond the river.

1562
01:05:51,510 --> 01:05:55,020
He's been to paradise, but
he's never been to me.

1563
01:05:55,010 --> 01:05:56,510
No.

1564
01:05:56,520 --> 01:05:59,020
If you break the law again, the
people will give you death.

1565
01:05:59,020 --> 01:06:00,520
I prefer liberty.

1566
01:06:02,520 --> 01:06:04,530
I shouldn't give you my voice
until you"ve been born again

1567
01:06:04,520 --> 01:06:06,020
after the rites of manhood.

1568
01:06:06,020 --> 01:06:07,520
Oh, she must be Baptist.

1569
01:06:07,530 --> 01:06:09,530
Wonder no more.

1570
01:06:09,530 --> 01:06:11,030
