All of this.

2101
01:29:34,530 --> 01:29:36,540
Are these symbols too?

2102
01:29:37,030 --> 01:29:38,030
Perhaps.

2103
01:29:38,540 --> 01:29:39,540
Maybe.

2104
01:29:40,040 --> 01:29:42,040
Someday they must be known.

2105
01:29:44,040 --> 01:29:46,050
It is a thing of wonder.

2106
01:29:46,040 --> 01:29:49,040
Yeah, I wonder when the
film's gonna end.

2107
01:29:51,550 --> 01:29:54,550
Shall we take him to the cave
and make a cairn for him?

2108
01:29:54,550 --> 01:29:56,060
Nah, let's eat 'em here.

2109
01:29:56,050 --> 01:29:58,050
Leave them in this
place that was his.

2110
01:29:58,060 --> 01:30:01,060
The people have seen, a
new law is made.

2111
01:30:01,060 --> 01:30:04,060
Food will be gathered,
wheel things made,

2112
01:30:04,060 --> 01:30:07,570
and the clan will seek out other
men in other places.

2113
01:30:07,560 --> 01:30:09,560
Other voices, other rooms.

2114
01:30:09,570 --> 01:30:10,570
We'll take this thing of wonder.

2115
01:30:11,570 --> 01:30:14,570
Somewhere a man may be able to
tell us the words.

2116
01:30:14,570 --> 01:30:15,580
Hey, Bob!

2117
01:30:15,570 --> 01:30:17,070
Bob, wake up, Bob.

2118
01:30:17,070 --> 01:30:18,070
There.

2119
01:30:18,080 --> 01:30:19,580
Or one of us may find
a way to know.

2120
01:30:20,080 --> 01:30:21,580
I bet his initials are
Robert Vaughn.

2121
01:30:21,580 --> 01:30:22,580
Aye.

2122
01:30:24,080 --> 01:30:25,590
So let this man stay.

2123
01:30:26,080 --> 01:30:28,080
He will not be alone.

2124
01:30:30,590 --> 01:30:33,590
Well, this guy's getting ripe,
let's get out of here.

2125
01:30:37,590 --> 01:30:39,090
So, bye.

2126
01:30:41,600 --> 01:30:43,100
Hey I just thought of something.

2127
01:30:43,100 --> 01:30:45,610
Who's gonna play the
Indian on F Troop?

2128
01:30:46,600 --> 01:30:48,600
<i>(Man): I and a party
of 23 others...</i>

2129
01:30:48,610 --> 01:30:50,110
What?

2130
01:30:50,110 --> 01:30:51,610
<i>...were on a
scientific expedition</i>

2131
01:30:51,610 --> 01:30:53,110
<i>when the bombs began to fall.</i>

2132
01:30:53,110 --> 01:30:54,610
- Oh. - Oh, message!

2133
01:30:54,610 --> 01:30:56,620
Message coming in, people.

2134
01:30:56,610 --> 01:30:58,110
I think it's from
Beach Dickerson.

2135
01:30:58,120 --> 01:31:00,120
<i>...was unleashed all
over the world.</i>

2136
01:31:00,120 --> 01:31:02,620
<i>Retaliation added to
retaliation.</i>

2137
01:31:02,620 --> 01:31:04,120
Oh, I see a president's face.

2138
01:31:04,120 --> 01:31:07,630
<i>Until all traces of man's
works had been wiped</i>

2139
01:31:07,620 --> 01:31:08,620
<i>from the face of the Earth.</i>

2140
01:31:08,630 --> 01:31:10,130
Sorry everyone, sorry.

2141
01:31:10,130 --> 01:31:11,630
I'm hot, I'm on fire.

2142
01:31:11,630 --> 01:31:14,130
(clicking noises)

2143
01:31:14,130 --> 01:31:17,140
<i>Some grew huge
beyond all reason</i>

2144
01:31:17,130 --> 01:31:19,630
<i>and formed as the
dinosaurs of prehistory,</i>

2145
01:31:19,640 --> 01:31:22,140
<i>or took on new
shapes altogether,</i>

2146
01:31:22,140 --> 01:31:24,140
<i>mad in shape and purpose.</i>

2147
01:31:24,140 --> 01:31:26,150
They became stock footage.

2148
01:31:26,140 --> 01:31:27,640
<i>My comrades and I,
half-protected</i>

2149
01:31:27,640 --> 01:31:31,140
<i>by our radiation suits, found
ourselves given an age</i>

2150
01:31:31,150 --> 01:31:33,650
<i>far beyond the span allowed.</i>

2151
01:31:33,650 --> 01:31:34,650
Hm.

2152
01:31:34,650 --> 01:31:36,160
<i>Out of all the
sprawling millions</i>

2153
01:31:36,650 --> 01:31:39,650
<i>of the Earth a handful
escaped all harm</i>

2154
01:31:39,660 --> 01:31:41,660
<i>through fortune or design.</i>

2155
01:31:41,660 --> 01:31:43,160
Oh, kinda like Neil Bush.

2156
01:31:43,160 --> 01:31:45,670
<i>After the holocaust, the
wisest of them</i>

2157
01:31:45,660 --> 01:31:48,660
set down a long list of taboos.

2158
01:31:48,670 --> 01:31:50,170
Am I the wisest?

2159
01:31:50,170 --> 01:31:51,170
Yeah, I'm the wisest.

2160
01:31:51,670 --> 01:31:52,670
Pretty much.

2161
01:31:52,670 --> 01:31:54,670
<i>The laws are in the form of
a religion now.</i>

2162
01:31:54,670 --> 01:31:58,180
It's strange to see them living
<i>the life of Cro-Magnon man.</i>

2163
01:31:58,180 --> 01:32:00,180
Cro-Magnon, P.I.

2164
01:32:01,180 --> 01:32:04,180
<i>On occasion we tried to
contact them,</i>

2165
01:32:04,180 --> 01:32:06,190
<i>but they feared us.</i>

2166
01:32:06,680 --> 01:32:07,680
Wonder why.

2167
01:32:07,680 --> 01:32:09,180
<i>And our radiation killed those</i>

2168
01:32:09,190 --> 01:32:10,690
<i>who came too close.</i>

2169
01:32:10,690 --> 01:32:12,690
<i>Now, only I'm left,</i>

2170
01:32:12,690 --> 01:32:17,200
and the radiation has worn away
<i>these long, long years.</i>

2171
01:32:17,190 --> 01:32:19,190
So you know it's okay.

2172
01:32:19,200 --> 01:32:21,200
<i>Now a new one
thinks and wonders</i>

2173
01:32:21,200 --> 01:32:23,200
<i>about the truth of the law.</i>

2174
01:32:23,200 --> 01:32:24,700
He's a real goosester!

2175
01:32:24,700 --> 01:32:27,210
<i>Perhaps man will dare
to try again.</i>

2176
01:32:27,200 --> 01:32:29,200
<i>I am very lonely.</i>

2177
01:32:29,210 --> 01:32:31,210
In fact, I'm dead.

2178
01:32:31,210 --> 01:32:33,210
<i>Very, very tired.</i>

2179
01:32:33,210 --> 01:32:34,710
Dead tired.

2180
01:32:35,710 --> 01:32:37,210
<i>This happened a long time ago.</i>

2181
01:32:37,210 --> 01:32:38,210
(humming)

2182
01:32:38,720 --> 01:32:41,220
<i>And as you know, men did
meet other men.</i>

2183
01:32:41,220 --> 01:32:44,220
<i>And fire smelted metal,
made explosives.</i>

2184
01:32:44,220 --> 01:32:47,730
<i>The wheel turned machines and
made gun barrels.</i>

2185
01:32:47,720 --> 01:32:50,720
<i>The towers were built
and flattened.</i>

2186
01:32:50,730 --> 01:32:53,230
<i>How many times?</i>

2187
01:32:53,230 --> 01:32:55,230
<i>Will it happen again?</i>

2188
01:32:56,230 --> 01:33:01,230
And if it does, will any at all
<i>survive the next time?</i>

2189
01:33:01,240 --> 01:33:03,740
Doubtful, let's go.

2190
01:33:03,740 --> 01:33:06,250
<i>Or will it be the end?</i>

2191
01:33:06,240 --> 01:33:07,240
Heavy.

2192
01:33:07,240 --> 01:33:08,240
Robert Vaughn will be back

2193
01:33:08,250 --> 01:33:10,250
in the Sweet Sweetback Affair!

2194
01:33:26,200 --> 01:33:28,200
Aye, I am the last survivor

2195
01:33:28,200 --> 01:33:30,200
of a movie-watching experiment!

2196
01:33:30,200 --> 01:33:31,200
Me too!

2197
01:33:31,200 --> 01:33:32,710
Oh yeah, him too!

2198
01:33:32,700 --> 01:33:33,700
Sh, character.

2199
01:33:33,700 --> 01:33:35,200
Whether through
fortune or design,

2200
01:33:35,210 --> 01:33:36,710
we are the only survivors.

2201
01:33:36,710 --> 01:33:39,210
The awesome power of Roger
Corman was unleashed

2202
01:33:39,210 --> 01:33:41,710
upon the satellite and
scared everybody!

2203
01:33:41,710 --> 01:33:44,220
it was brought upon us
by scientists

2204
01:33:44,210 --> 01:33:45,710
mad in shape and purpose.

2205
01:33:45,720 --> 01:33:47,220
Aye, aye.

2206
01:33:47,220 --> 01:33:48,220
And the fact that I am dead
does not prevent me

2207
01:33:48,220 --> 01:33:49,720
from tying up a few loose ends.

2208
01:33:49,720 --> 01:33:51,220
Me too, you keep
forgetting about me!

2209
01:33:51,220 --> 01:33:52,220
Oh yeah, him too.

2210
01:33:52,220 --> 01:33:52,730
Sh, character.

2211
01:33:52,720 --> 01:33:54,220
Aye!

2212
01:33:54,220 --> 01:33:56,220
I have, protected by our
Trumpy radiation suits,

2213
01:33:56,230 --> 01:33:57,230
wait for contact.

2214
01:33:57,230 --> 01:33:59,230
Hey, hi guys, what's up?

2215
01:33:59,230 --> 01:34:00,730
Human!

2216
01:34:00,730 --> 01:34:02,230
Oh, you guys, come on.

2217
01:34:02,230 --> 01:34:05,240
Aye, he was the young one
who began to wonder.

2218
01:34:05,240 --> 01:34:07,740
I'm starting to wonder
about these two.

2219
01:34:07,740 --> 01:34:10,740
He was unfettered by a long
list of taboos,

2220
01:34:10,740 --> 01:34:13,750
except that he refused to
wear silly hats.

2221
01:34:13,740 --> 01:34:15,240
Listen, are you guys
supposed to be dead?

2222
01:34:15,250 --> 01:34:16,750
You know, I can see
your lips move.

2223
01:34:17,250 --> 01:34:20,250
Aye, we refuse to ad lib and
give in to his demands

2224
01:34:20,250 --> 01:34:23,760
and smell his feet, which were
like bad meat or good cheese!

2225
01:34:23,750 --> 01:34:25,750
Oh come on you guys, quit
your clowning.

2226
01:34:25,760 --> 01:34:27,260
I'm supposed to read the letter,
okay?

2227
01:34:27,260 --> 01:34:29,760
One took great pleasure in
reading letters.

2228
01:34:29,760 --> 01:34:30,760
Aye.

2229
01:34:30,760 --> 01:34:31,260
Where is it?

2230
01:34:31,260 --> 01:34:32,260
It's supposed to be here.

2231
01:34:32,760 --> 01:34:34,260
Letter, letter! It's the the
radiation suits!

2232
01:34:34,260 --> 01:34:35,760
Letter, letter!

2233
01:34:35,770 --> 01:34:37,770
Oh, geez, come on!

2234
01:34:37,770 --> 01:34:39,270
Tickle the old ones.

2235
01:34:39,770 --> 01:34:41,270
Sorry about the slime,
young one.

2236
01:34:41,770 --> 01:34:45,280
It's covered in slime and this
matted monkey hair,

2237
01:34:45,280 --> 01:34:48,280
fake monkey hair that you made
these suits out of.

2238
01:34:48,780 --> 01:34:50,780
It comes with the territory,
young one.

2239
01:34:50,780 --> 01:34:56,290
Okay, well, let's put this
on still, Cambot.

2240
01:34:57,790 --> 01:34:58,790
You got that?

2241
01:34:58,790 --> 01:35:00,290
Well this is a pretty neat one,

2242
01:35:00,290 --> 01:35:01,790
before it got slimed.

2243
01:35:01,790 --> 01:35:04,800
It's from Bruce Barber,
and it says,

2244
01:35:04,790 --> 01:35:07,290
"Verify ye hence and
testify furthermore,

2245
01:35:07,800 --> 01:35:09,300
"that your show has a large
and loyal following

2246
01:35:09,300 --> 01:35:11,300
"among the professional
stuntmen here in L.A.

2247
01:35:11,300 --> 01:35:13,810
"Nothing brings home
to us exactly

2248
01:35:13,800 --> 01:35:15,800
"how far the stunt
business has come,

2249
01:35:15,810 --> 01:35:17,310
"as watching the action

2250
01:35:17,310 --> 01:35:19,810
"on some of the turkeys you
have graced us with.

2251
01:35:19,810 --> 01:35:21,310
"I try never to miss a show.

2252
01:35:21,310 --> 01:35:22,820
"The wife, who thinks
I'm sick..."

2253
01:35:22,810 --> 01:35:23,810
The wife?

2254
01:35:23,810 --> 01:35:24,810
- The wife? (chuckles) -
"...tapes them for me

2255
01:35:25,320 --> 01:35:26,320
"when I'm on location.

2256
01:35:26,320 --> 01:35:28,320
"Please keep up the good,
bad work."

2257
01:35:28,320 --> 01:35:29,820
Bruce Barber.

2258
01:35:29,820 --> 01:35:30,820
Pretty neat, huh?

2259
01:35:30,820 --> 01:35:32,320
Aye.

2260
01:35:32,320 --> 01:35:33,330
You guys are gonna have to clean
all this up, you know.

2261
01:35:33,320 --> 01:35:34,820
Again with the taboo.

2262
01:35:34,820 --> 01:35:35,820
Nay, nay!

2263
01:35:36,330 --> 01:35:37,830
Just be quiet, we gotta
get outta here.

2264
01:35:38,330 --> 01:35:39,830
What do you think, sirs?

2265
01:35:39,830 --> 01:35:42,330
Mm, that is good.

2266
01:35:43,830 --> 01:35:46,330
I'm glad I brought the
orange cappuccino.

2267
01:35:46,340 --> 01:35:49,340
Wait a minute, I brought the
orange cappuccino.

2268
01:35:49,340 --> 01:35:51,340
(laughing)

2269
01:35:51,340 --> 01:35:52,850
(wincing)

2270
01:35:54,340 --> 01:35:57,340
Oh, hello bubbie, Frank and I
are just patching things up

2271
01:35:57,350 --> 01:35:59,350
with a little cup of kindness.

2272
01:36:02,350 --> 01:36:03,360
You know, it's the quiet moments

2273
01:36:03,350 --> 01:36:05,350
that are the most
precious moments.

2274
01:36:05,360 --> 01:36:06,860
Mm.

2275
01:36:06,860 --> 01:36:08,860
Why don't you push the button,
Frank?

2276
01:36:08,860 --> 01:36:12,360
I'm going to slip this tape of
Dad in with Jack Lemmon.

2277
01:36:12,360 --> 01:36:15,370
I think we could both use a
good cry, don't you?

2278
01:36:15,370 --> 01:36:16,870
I'll make some popcorn.

2279
01:36:21,370 --> 01:36:23,380
(laughing)

2280
01:36:23,370 --> 01:36:25,870
(pained groans)

2281
01:36:29,150 --> 01:36:33,150
(majestic music)

